# D-Bus activation for AnyFlow's desktop application.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why this file exists
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The desktop entry has carried `DBusActivatable=true` since the Quick Panel
# sprint, and the GtkApplication has exported `app.quick-panel`,
# `app.settings` and `app.transfers` on the session bus since then too. That
# is enough for a caller to raise a surface of an AnyFlow that is *already
# running*. It is not enough to start one, and the difference was measured
# rather than assumed:
#
#     $ pkill -x anyflow-gui
#     $ gdbus call --session --dest io.github.yurisismotto.anyflow \
#           --object-path /io/github/yurisismotto/anyflow \
#           --method org.freedesktop.Application.ActivateAction \
#           quick-panel '[]' '{}'
#     Error: org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.ServiceUnknown: The name is not activatable
#
# `DBusActivatable=true` is a promise *about* the application, read by things
# that launch desktop entries. The message bus does not read desktop entries;
# it reads this directory. Without an entry here the bus has no way to start
# the name, which is why the call above fails while the identical call against
# a running instance succeeds.
#
# The tray item needs the cold case: someone clicks AnyFlow in the system tray
# on a freshly booted session, where `anyflowd` is running as a user service
# and no GUI process exists at all.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why `--gapplication-service`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Without it, the bus starts `anyflow-gui` with no arguments, which is a bare
# launch — and a bare launch opens Settings. The person who clicked "Quick
# Panel" would get two windows, one of them unasked for. With it, GApplication
# enters service mode: it registers the bus name, opens nothing, and waits for
# the activation message that is already on its way. Measured on this build:
# the process owns `io.github.yurisismotto.anyflow`, exports no window object,
# and exits by itself after ten idle seconds.
#
# That last part is the lifecycle this whole sprint is built to protect. The
# GUI does not become resident in order to have a tray icon; it is started for
# a window and it leaves when the window is gone. `anyflowd` stays the only
# long-lived AnyFlow process, and it is the daemon — not this — that owns the
# StatusNotifierItem.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @BINDIR@
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `Exec` in a D-Bus service file must be an absolute path; the bus does not
# search `PATH`. It is substituted at install time from the prefix the
# installer was given, so a development install under `~/.local` and a package
# under `/usr` produce the same file with the one line that has to differ.
# Nothing here is written by hand and no repository path can reach it.
[D-BUS Service]
Name=io.github.yurisismotto.anyflow
Exec=@BINDIR@/anyflow-gui --gapplication-service
